<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Giang Vo by Motorbike: Motorbike Route Connections in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Giang Vo&rsquo;s riding story is a story of connections, because the boulevard quarter of Ba Dinh&rsquo;s western side is a hinge between two cities, the landmark precincts and the old centre eastward, the working districts and the modern west southward and onward, and the rental counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien across the whole map on the river&rsquo;s far side. A rider based here is connected to everything by short, legible legs, and the skill the quarter asks is the planner&rsquo;s small one, knowing which line serves which trip and at which hour. This page reads those connections honestly, without fabricated journey times, because duration is the day&rsquo;s own fact and the honest guide teaches the shape, not the stopwatch.</p>
<p>The rental counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River, and the connection to it is the plan&rsquo;s spine. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/ba-dinh-route-connections/">Ba Dinh route connections</a> page for the district-level network, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/dong-da-route-connections/">Dong Da route connections</a> page for the working district to the south.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
